      "title": "prove: verify task stack-size parsing",
      "body": "Verify decimal parsing of the build-time task stack size: for decimal input\nfitting in `u32`, return its exact value without indexing or arithmetic panics.\nPreserve empty input as zero, absent input as the supplied default, arbitrary\nleading zeroes, and both `const fn` signatures.\n\nExtract the two parsers into private `task::stack_size` because `kernel_stack`\nis currently disabled and cannot be verified in place without enabling its\nlarger dependency closure. Keep their executable bodies unchanged and preserve\nthe originals in an `Origin Rust:` block. The wrapper becomes `pub(super)` so\nthe sibling caller can use it, without adding a crate public API.\n\nThe disabled `option_env!` initializer's decimal/range obligation remains\ndocumented as a TODO. The wrapper has a narrow `expect(dead_code)` while that\ncaller is disabled.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Isolated exact-source proof and erased library compilation: 5 verified,\n  0 errors. Portable relative-path entry: `tools/tests/stack_size.rs`.\n- Rust 1.99.1; Asterinas Verus revision\n  `bdb1aed60228c454f959f45d6a98dec5dfdf2a92`.\n- From the repository root, run the isolated entry using that built toolchain:\n\n  ```sh\n  tools/verus/source/target-verus/release/verus tools/tests/stack_size.rs \\\n    --crate-type lib --verify-only-module stack_size --multiple-errors 5\n  ```\n\n  On Windows, use `verus.exe`. This loads the repository source directly through\n  a relative path. The isolated entry does not verify kernel-stack allocation\n  or the environment-dependent static initializer.\n- Full OSTD verification remains blocked: a same-toolchain check of original\n  HEAD sources and the modified crate yields the same sequence of 129 existing\n  `verus_spec(with ...)` call-resolution errors. This is not an integration pass.\n- Scoped Verus formatting and diff checks pass; proof simplification retained\n  the required hints.\n",
      "url": "https://github.com/asterinas/vostd/pull/906",
